        			<p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in"><span style="font-size:14px"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">Notes:</span></span></p>
        
        			<p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in"><span style="font-size:14px"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><sup>1</sup>Additional right-of-way may be required if roadside swales are used to control storm drainage, for bike lanes if designated on the plan, or for wider sidewalks depending on the zoning.</span></span></p>
        
        			<p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in"><span style="font-size:14px"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><sup>2</sup>Lanes can be through lanes, turn pockets, or continuous TWLTL.</span></span></p>
        
        			<p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in"><span style="font-size:14px"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><sup>3</sup>Curb-to-curb width varies depending on street features including number of lanes, on-street parking, bike lane, median and turn lanes.&nbsp; See Design Standards for more detail.</span></span></p>
